This repository's original code (everything outside `src/tts/sparc/`) is licensed under the
MIT License below.

The code in `src/tts/sparc/` is adapted from the author's own fork
(https://github.com/nzxyin/Speech-Articulatory-Coding) of the SPARC (Speech Articulatory Coding)
codebase, itself based on the official implementation by Cheol Jun Cho, Peter Wu, Tejas S.
Prabhune, Dhruv Agarwal, and Gopala K. Anumanchipalli (Berkeley Speech Group), released without
an explicit license. Its use and modification here is with the original authors' direct
permission, granted in response to a licensing inquiry. If you use this software, please cite
the original paper:

Cheol Jun Cho, Peter Wu, Tejas S. Prabhune, Dhruv Agarwal, and Gopala K. Anumanchipalli, "Coding
Speech through Vocal Tract Kinematics," IEEE Journal of Selected Topics in Signal Processing,
vol. 18, no. 8, pp. 1427-1440, 2024. https://arxiv.org/abs/2406.12998

`src/tts/sparc/generator.py` is additionally based on the HiFi-GAN implementation by Jungil Kong
(https://github.com/jik876/hifi-gan), released under the MIT License:

